1️⃣ Problem Statement

We are dealing with a medical claims Accounts Payable (AP) process.

Claims come from a claims system, but payment is not immediate.
They must go through multiple steps involving:

Claim submission

Internal review

Consolidation

Treasury payment

Treasury acknowledgment (success / failure)

Core Challenges

Claims change state over time

Submitted → Under Review → Approved / Rejected

Payment happens externally (Treasury)

Feedback comes later via files

Same claim must be updated, not duplicated

System must always show the latest truth

Pipeline should be restart-safe and idempotent

Files can arrive late or be reprocessed

Auditability and correctness are critical

So the real problem is:

How do we build a reliable, end-to-end medical claims AP system that can ingest files, update claim state correctly, interact with Treasury, and always expose the latest status?

2️⃣ What We Are Trying to Solve

We want to build a solution that:

✔ Handles continuous file arrivals
✔ Updates existing claims cleanly (UPSERT)
✔ Supports two-direction data flow
✔ Separates ingestion from business logic
✔ Avoids duplicates and data corruption
✔ Works in production scale

In short:

A robust, stateful claims payment system using modern Databricks patterns.

3️⃣ Solution Overview (High Level)

We designed the system around two logical cycles:

✅ First Half Cycle – Send claims to Treasury
✅ Second Half Cycle – Receive acknowledgment and finalize claims

The entire system is built using:

Delta Live Tables (DLT)

Auto Loader

SCD Type 1 (UPSERT)

Clear Bronze → Silver → Gold flow

4️⃣ First Half Cycle – Claim Intake → Payment Request
🔹 Step 1: Claim Source Data Arrives

We receive multiple claim-related files:

Claim Header

Claim Line

Diagnosis

Approval (Reviewer)

These files are raw, file-based inputs.

🔹 Step 2: Bronze Layer – Raw Ingestion

What we did:

Used Auto Loader

Read files exactly as received

No transformation, no validation

Why:

Preserve source data

Handle incremental file arrival

Auto schema tracking

Restart-safe ingestion

👉 Bronze acts as the system of record for source files

🔹 Step 3: Silver Layer – Business State (SCD-1)

This is the heart of the system.

What problem exists here?

Claims can be resent

Updates may arrive later

Same claim ID must not create duplicates

What we did:

Converted Silver tables to SCD Type 1 (UPSERT)

Used dlt.create_auto_cdc_flow

Introduced CDC staging tables

Ensured:

One row per business key

Latest state always wins

Design choice:

Silver is an operational state layer, not a history layer.

So:

Claim Header = latest claim state

Claim Lines / Diagnosis / Approval = latest version

🔹 Step 4: Gold Layer – Treasury Payment Request

Gold represents actionable business output.

What we did:

Joined Silver Claim Header

Aggregated Claim Lines to compute payable amount

Built one payment request per claim

Created a Treasury-ready dataset

👉 This Gold table is what we send out of Databricks to Treasury.

✅ At this point, first half of the AP cycle is complete.

5️⃣ Second Half Cycle – Treasury ACK → Final Settlement
🔹 Step 5: Treasury Sends Payment ACK File

Treasury sends back a file containing:

Payment ID

Claim ID

Payment Status (Confirmed / Failed)

Bank reference or failure reason

Acknowledgment status

This is the final authority on payment outcome.

🔹 Step 6: Bronze – ACK Ingestion

We again use:

✅ Auto Loader
✅ Bronze landing table

ACK files are treated as external system truth, not transformations.

🔹 Step 7: Silver – SCD-1 UPSERT from ACK

This is where the system becomes complete.

What we did:

Mapped ACK status to claim lifecycle:

SUCCESS → Approved / Paid

REJECTED → Rejected / Not Paid

Used Auto CDC again

Updated the same Silver Claim Header table

✅ No new claim rows
✅ Same claim updated
✅ Always one final state

This ensures:

The claim table always reflects the real-world payment outcome.

🔹 Step 8: Gold – Final Truth

Because Gold is derived from Silver:

It automatically reflects:

Approved claims

Rejected claims

Payment references

Failure reasons

Gold becomes the single source of truth for:

Finance

Reporting

Audit

Reconciliation

6️⃣ Why This Is a Complete Solution

This design solves all original problems:

✅ Handles continuous files
✅ Prevents duplicates
✅ Supports retries and reprocessing
✅ Keeps latest claim state
✅ Clean separation of concerns
✅ Works with external systems
✅ Production-safe architecture
✅ Easy to explain and extend

7️⃣ Final Architecture Summary (One Slide)
Claims Source Files
        ↓
Bronze (Auto Loader – Raw)
        ↓
Silver (SCD-1 – Operational State)
        ↓
Gold (Payment Requests)
        ↓
Treasury
        ↓
ACK Files
        ↓
Silver (UPSERT Final Status)
        ↓
Gold (Final Settlement Truth)